<subpara id="RM000000DG800OX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___000027100000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>Air Conditioner Amplifier Assembly (A/C ECU)</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Disconnect the air conditioner amplifier assembly connector.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage and resistance of each terminal of the vehicle side wire harness connector.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E132743J03" width="7.106578999in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.33in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.95in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.8in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Terminal Symbol]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A1←→A14</ptxt>
<ptxt>[IG+←→GND]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A14 ←→ Body ground</ptxt>
<ptxt>[GND ←→ Body ground]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A21←→A14</ptxt>
<ptxt>[B←→GND]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>If the result is not as specified, there may be a malfunction on the vehicle side.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Connect the air conditioner amplifier assembly connector.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage of each terminal of the connector. Also, when checking pulses, use an oscilloscope.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
